WEBVTT

00:16.200 --> 00:17.120
♪ Oh ♪

00:17.200 --> 00:18.120
[breathing heavily]

00:18.200 --> 00:19.360
♪ Show ♪

00:20.760 --> 00:23.800
♪ Tell me I'm the only one ♪

00:24.840 --> 00:25.880
♪ Yeah ♪

00:26.960 --> 00:28.080
♪ Show ♪

00:28.800 --> 00:32.200
♪ I didn't know ♪

00:33.200 --> 00:34.560
Happy or sad, Tommy?

00:34.640 --> 00:35.480
♪ Show ♪

00:37.280 --> 00:40.760
♪ Tell me you're the one I can call ♪

00:41.640 --> 00:46.640
♪ Even if you choke ♪

00:50.480 --> 00:51.560
[boat engine chugging]

00:59.360 --> 01:00.200
[gun clicks]

01:00.840 --> 01:02.160
Mr Shelby.

01:02.240 --> 01:03.080
[loading gun]

01:04.280 --> 01:08.240
My bullets ache
to get inside your tinker head.

01:10.560 --> 01:13.160
♪ Up to our knees in Fenian blood ♪

01:13.240 --> 01:15.520
♪ Surrender or you'll die ♪

01:16.000 --> 01:19.880
♪ We are the Brigton Derry Billy Boys ♪

01:19.960 --> 01:22.080
[gun firing]

01:35.680 --> 01:36.520
[scoffs]

01:39.920 --> 01:40.760
[sniffles]

01:55.040 --> 01:56.240
You know, it's a pity.

01:56.920 --> 01:58.880
I was looking forward to killing you.

02:00.520 --> 02:02.120
You're at the back of a long queue.

02:04.440 --> 02:06.720
My white flag is a flag of truce.

02:08.200 --> 02:10.000
Yours is more a flag of surrender.

02:11.600 --> 02:13.440
Whatever you say, Mr McCavern.

02:13.520 --> 02:15.600
Colour is the same,
the outcome is the same.

02:16.640 --> 02:20.360
I believe we have friends in common.
We should postpone our war.

02:20.440 --> 02:22.760
Your brother left me a hand grenade.

02:22.840 --> 02:24.320
He sends his apologies.

02:25.080 --> 02:26.400
You left me landmines.

02:27.320 --> 02:29.240
For which I, too, apologise.

02:30.320 --> 02:31.560
Then peace it is.

02:32.520 --> 02:35.760
Your message said you wanted to
seal our truce with some business.

02:37.480 --> 02:40.680
Since we're men of similar interests
and distribution networks,

02:40.760 --> 02:43.440
I thought we might use
our temporary settlement

02:43.520 --> 02:44.840
for our mutual benefit.

02:45.640 --> 02:48.560
You stand in a yard full of scrap metal
and stolen goods

02:48.640 --> 02:50.320
and you talk like a politician.

02:50.400 --> 02:53.600
No. Nothing here is stolen, Mr McCavern.

02:53.680 --> 02:56.360
Charlie simply finds things
before they're lost.

02:58.680 --> 03:01.400
The nature of the deal
is explained in my proposal.

03:02.480 --> 03:05.600
I've booked you a suite
at the Midland Hotel.

03:06.160 --> 03:08.760
If you need anything in this city,
just mention my name.

03:09.840 --> 03:11.760
So you want to impress me, Mr Shelby?

03:13.200 --> 03:14.360
Isiah.

03:17.920 --> 03:19.880
Also in the envelope is a cheque...

03:20.880 --> 03:22.880
for £500. For your wife.

03:22.960 --> 03:25.200
She can use it to buy a black dress,

03:26.280 --> 03:28.640
rent a black horse with black feathers,

03:29.280 --> 03:31.720
to pull a black carriage
with your body in it,

03:32.240 --> 03:35.160
should you break the terms
of the white flag.

03:36.360 --> 03:40.960
Now, please, enjoy the city
it's my honor to represent.

04:04.520 --> 04:07.200
This week, I managed to get
to the people, York and Lincoln City.

04:07.280 --> 04:08.880
I mean, they're the teams that will lose.

04:09.480 --> 04:10.720
I got to the...

04:11.840 --> 04:14.160
All right. Go on, go on. Take your time.

04:14.240 --> 04:15.600
-Hmm?
-[Billy inhales shakily]

04:17.000 --> 04:20.120
I got to the goalkeepers.
They all said five pounds is enough. I...

04:22.560 --> 04:23.399
[exhales heavily]

04:23.480 --> 04:26.640
I've written to the, um, people
at Tranmere Rovers

04:26.720 --> 04:29.760
because the phone you put
into my house has stopped working.

04:29.840 --> 04:32.000
-So I'm gonna need another one of those.
-[Arthur] Okay.

04:32.640 --> 04:35.040
Once we've got that fixed, eh,

04:35.720 --> 04:40.960
then we'll have all the names and numbers
of the first division referees.

04:42.000 --> 04:43.600
-The first?
-Yeah!

04:44.240 --> 04:47.080
[sobbing] Shit. Ah, shit.
Shit, shit, shit...

04:47.160 --> 04:49.800
Billy. Come on. Come on, listen.
Listen to me.

04:50.600 --> 04:52.120
Come on, now.

04:52.200 --> 04:54.960
-No need for that. Hmm?
-Hmm. Yeah.

04:55.040 --> 04:57.160
We need you to find out what they like.

04:57.840 --> 04:59.680
You know, what gets them going.

05:00.840 --> 05:04.160
'Cause a lot of them are comfortable.
A fiver's nothing to them.

05:04.240 --> 05:06.480
We need you to find out
what they really like, Billy.

05:06.560 --> 05:07.400
Yes.

05:07.480 --> 05:09.440
See, 'cause we can offer them that.

05:10.280 --> 05:11.840
Yeah, Shelby Company Limited.

05:11.920 --> 05:16.000
We can offer them
all the lovely things people like.

05:16.760 --> 05:17.600
Hmm?

05:18.160 --> 05:20.440
We can also offer 'em protection

05:21.280 --> 05:23.440
from the things they don't like.

05:24.760 --> 05:26.520
You ever touch my family...

05:27.800 --> 05:29.040
ever...

05:32.480 --> 05:33.840
York...

05:34.320 --> 05:36.080
-Hmm. Lincoln.
-[mouthing] Lincoln.

05:36.160 --> 05:37.000
[Arthur] Hmm.

05:40.080 --> 05:41.480
Tranmere Rovers.

05:42.120 --> 05:42.960
Hmm?

05:43.600 --> 05:44.440
[Finn chuckles]

05:45.880 --> 05:46.920
Bye, Finn.

05:47.480 --> 05:48.520
Goodbye, brother.

05:49.520 --> 05:50.560
[door opens]

05:50.640 --> 05:51.600
[whispering] Shit.

05:52.800 --> 05:53.640
[door closes]

06:10.480 --> 06:13.880
[Tommy] It's all right, Mrs Conners,
you can carry on. It's just me brother.

06:17.360 --> 06:18.880
So, tell me how it happened.

06:19.560 --> 06:21.440
[Mrs Conners] Uh, they were
sleeping downstairs,

06:22.640 --> 06:24.360
and then my husband came home,

06:25.520 --> 06:28.080
drunk from the Marquis
even though he'd just lost his job.

06:28.160 --> 06:29.200
We don't have any money.

06:31.040 --> 06:33.560
Anyway... he came to bed.

06:34.080 --> 06:37.360
But downstairs, they must've
heard a noise. They woke up.

06:37.920 --> 06:39.640
They started, uh, calling out.

06:41.320 --> 06:42.800
They woke my husband up...

06:43.800 --> 06:45.880
and when he's drunk,
you don't wake him up.

06:47.600 --> 06:49.520
What happened then, Mrs Conners?

06:51.040 --> 06:51.880
[Mrs Conners] He, uh...

06:52.800 --> 06:53.720
He...

06:54.840 --> 06:56.200
He went downstairs.

06:58.720 --> 06:59.560
[whispering] He killed them.

07:01.680 --> 07:03.480
Strangled them, all three of them.

07:05.920 --> 07:07.160
And you've, um...

07:09.000 --> 07:11.520
you've brought
their bodies here today with you?

07:12.840 --> 07:14.600
Proof, Mr Shelby.

07:27.080 --> 07:27.920
[scoffs]

07:28.000 --> 07:31.040
Their singing
was the only pretty thing in my life.

07:33.560 --> 07:35.680
I don't care my husband beats me...

07:37.680 --> 07:39.000
but not this.

07:41.560 --> 07:44.120
Mrs Conners, we have your address.

07:45.400 --> 07:47.520
We will speak to your husband.

07:48.440 --> 07:51.600
My brother here
will go to the Bull Ring Market today

07:51.680 --> 07:55.640
and buy you three new goldfinches
and have them delivered to your door.

07:55.720 --> 07:59.080
With the same colours
and, you know, feathers.

08:00.160 --> 08:03.280
The new ones
I will call Thomas, Arthur and Finn.

08:04.560 --> 08:07.920
That'll make him pause
even when he's drunk.

08:09.160 --> 08:10.400
Good day, Mr Shelby.

08:11.840 --> 08:13.600
-You take care, Mrs Conners.
-Bye.

08:18.440 --> 08:20.200
[scoffs] I don't know
how you do this, Tom.

08:20.280 --> 08:22.200
I really don't.

08:23.040 --> 08:24.640
You learn things, Arthur.

08:26.400 --> 08:29.400
That woman has only two rooms downstairs.

08:30.000 --> 08:33.240
Her husband has lost his job
and he beats her.

08:33.320 --> 08:37.600
And yet the thing that brings her
to see her Member of Parliament

08:38.840 --> 08:40.159
is songbirds.

08:41.600 --> 08:43.200
Now, that's politics, Arthur.

08:44.360 --> 08:45.480
It's not for me.

08:46.000 --> 08:48.200
Anyway, look. Our list of losers.

08:48.280 --> 08:50.080
[Tommy] How much
have we made on the football?

08:50.160 --> 08:51.480
Ten grand this week.

08:52.080 --> 08:55.440
Finn showing promise, Tom.
Maybe we should put him on the track.

08:56.000 --> 08:56.960
Just a thought.

08:57.560 --> 08:58.400
[snorts]

08:58.480 --> 09:00.200
-[knocking at door]
-[door opening]

09:00.280 --> 09:01.520
-Finn?
-Yeah?

09:01.600 --> 09:03.080
Your lunchtime delivery.

09:03.160 --> 09:04.400
Bring her in.

09:04.880 --> 09:05.720
[Finn sniffing]

09:11.440 --> 09:12.320
[Micky] Tommy.

09:12.920 --> 09:15.080
The next fellow wants to see both of ye.

09:16.400 --> 09:18.640
-Do you know his face?
-No. He's Chinese.

09:18.720 --> 09:19.560
[Tommy snorts]

09:20.240 --> 09:21.640
Chinese, in our pub?

09:25.720 --> 09:26.560
Tom.

09:28.320 --> 09:29.200
All right.

09:30.680 --> 09:32.280
Slowly, Micky. Let him in.

09:35.640 --> 09:36.720
Three little birds, eh?

09:38.080 --> 09:40.520
Tommy, Finn and Arthur.

09:47.400 --> 09:48.440
Mr Thomas.

09:52.200 --> 09:53.120
Mr Arthur.

09:53.200 --> 09:54.840
[inhales and exhales sharply]

09:55.480 --> 09:56.400
[door closes]

09:57.160 --> 09:58.000
[sighs]

10:01.640 --> 10:03.120
My name is Brilliant Chang.

10:05.920 --> 10:08.920
Brilliant Chang is dead.

10:09.680 --> 10:10.600
Perhaps.

10:12.680 --> 10:14.200
Sometimes, I wonder...

10:14.680 --> 10:15.760
is this heaven?

10:16.240 --> 10:17.080
[scoffs]

10:17.840 --> 10:18.760
[inhales sharply]

10:18.840 --> 10:20.480
Doesn't smell like heaven.

10:21.400 --> 10:24.160
So I would say I have survived.

10:27.520 --> 10:28.480
What happened to Maggie?

10:29.200 --> 10:30.680
You don't like me?

10:30.760 --> 10:31.840
[Finn sighs]

10:32.920 --> 10:34.120
I like everything.

10:37.440 --> 10:41.040
I like fucking everything.

10:43.720 --> 10:44.600
[phone ringing]

10:46.240 --> 10:47.080
[smacks lips]

10:47.560 --> 10:49.840
You should answer the phone, Mr Shelby.

10:54.880 --> 10:56.240
Micky, bring that phone here, now.

10:59.960 --> 11:02.640
-Hello?
-[Finn panting] Arthur! Arthur!

11:04.680 --> 11:07.720
I sent a woman with a gun
to your youngest brother's office.

11:08.720 --> 11:09.880
[Arthur] It's all right, Finn.

11:09.960 --> 11:11.080
[Finn shuddering] Wait, wait.

11:13.400 --> 11:15.200
What the fuck is going on?

11:19.200 --> 11:21.520
Do you wanna die again, Chang? Hmm?

11:24.040 --> 11:24.880
Good.

11:25.480 --> 11:26.520
The guns are pointed.

11:27.040 --> 11:29.080
Now we are all concentrating.

11:29.560 --> 11:31.360
The moment is now pure.

11:32.360 --> 11:36.680
Purity is not necessary.
Displays are not necessary.

11:36.760 --> 11:42.000
They said, "Tommy Shelby.
That door will need some kicking down."

11:44.080 --> 11:46.440
When you walked through that door,
it was open.

11:48.000 --> 11:50.520
You don't need to do anything
to get my attention.

11:51.360 --> 11:53.680
Now, what exactly do you want?

11:53.760 --> 11:54.600
[Chang sighs]

11:58.960 --> 12:01.440
Do you have a match, Mr Shelby?

12:06.160 --> 12:08.160
Anything happens to my brother, Chang...

12:09.840 --> 12:11.120
you die.

12:24.440 --> 12:25.280
[Chang inhales sharply]

12:25.840 --> 12:26.760
If you die here today,

12:26.840 --> 12:29.360
we'll bury you face-down with no hands.
You'll go straight to hell.

12:29.440 --> 12:31.640
I don't care about rituals.

12:32.560 --> 12:34.880
I am a rationalist, Mr Shelby.

12:35.640 --> 12:37.400
Well, tell your friend on the phone

12:38.200 --> 12:41.040
to put her gun down
and we can all have a talk.

12:45.000 --> 12:46.000
[gun fires over telephone]

12:46.080 --> 12:47.000
[Arthur breathing heavily]

12:47.560 --> 12:48.520
Hold your fire, brother.

12:49.640 --> 12:50.760
Hold your fire.

12:51.320 --> 12:52.200
[Finn breathing heavily]

12:55.360 --> 12:56.640
I'm all right.

12:56.720 --> 12:58.440
She fired into the ceiling.

12:58.520 --> 12:59.520
Finn's all right.

13:00.720 --> 13:01.840
Finn's okay.

13:03.640 --> 13:04.520
[sighs]

13:09.360 --> 13:11.520
Give me the order. Hmm?

13:12.440 --> 13:13.600
Give me the order, Tommy.

13:14.160 --> 13:15.760
-Yes or no?
-At ease.

13:19.480 --> 13:20.720
I said, at ease.

13:23.120 --> 13:24.640
[Arthur breathing heavily]

13:36.040 --> 13:38.920
May I take something
from my pocket, Mr Shelby?

14:07.680 --> 14:09.520
[exhales sharply and coughs]

14:10.520 --> 14:11.360
[sighs]

14:12.360 --> 14:16.640
It is the purest opium
that has ever arrived in Europe.

14:17.320 --> 14:19.120
No salt, no flour...

14:19.600 --> 14:20.440
no lies.

14:20.960 --> 14:22.600
Pure truth.

14:24.120 --> 14:28.400
Came off a ship called the Capital...
out of Shanghai.

14:29.000 --> 14:30.600
Docked at Poplar a week ago.

14:31.400 --> 14:33.440
Stevedores were held at gunpoint.

14:34.000 --> 14:37.480
Chinese unloaded the cargo
by the light of lanterns.

14:39.040 --> 14:41.400
A foreman at the dock estimated there was

14:41.960 --> 14:43.800
seven tons of the stuff.

14:43.880 --> 14:44.960
[Chang scoffs]

14:45.040 --> 14:46.840
I made a note at the time.

14:50.680 --> 14:52.400
I spoke to that particular foreman,

14:52.960 --> 14:54.760
and I worked out that

14:55.440 --> 14:58.920
seven tons of pure opium crystals
would be worth...

15:00.720 --> 15:05.400
approximately £1,190,000

15:06.240 --> 15:08.000
on international markets.

15:08.800 --> 15:09.680
[Chang chuckles]

15:11.520 --> 15:12.720
[inhales sharply]

15:12.800 --> 15:14.560
The big crash, hmm?

15:16.240 --> 15:17.760
Wall Street.

15:17.840 --> 15:21.200
Now we all
keep our ears open for opportunities.

15:26.960 --> 15:28.840
-What the fuck is going on?
-[Arthur] What are you doing?

15:28.920 --> 15:30.040
-[gun fires]
-Bastard.

15:30.120 --> 15:33.040
[Tommy] Finn, we are conducting
a piece of business.

15:33.120 --> 15:36.360
She had a gun to my fucking head!
[panting]

15:36.440 --> 15:38.160
But your trousers are dry.

15:38.240 --> 15:40.960
You didn't piss yourself.
He didn't piss himself, Arthur.

15:41.040 --> 15:42.240
Well done, Finn.

15:42.320 --> 15:45.240
You had a dispute with a lady
and you didn't piss yourself.

15:45.320 --> 15:48.080
And Arthur here tells me
we should put you on the tracks.

15:48.760 --> 15:50.960
It'll be a good day for you
after all, Finn.

15:51.040 --> 15:52.640
-Give me that.
-Hey.

15:53.240 --> 15:55.920
Always have your whores
searched at the door.

15:56.000 --> 15:59.040
[scoffs] If I see that bitch on
the street, I'll fucking cut her, yeah?

15:59.120 --> 16:00.480
Yeah, all right. Come on.

16:02.080 --> 16:02.920
[door closes]

16:03.840 --> 16:04.680
[Chang sighs]

16:07.200 --> 16:09.720
This is a gift, Mr Shelby.

16:11.960 --> 16:13.400
Gesture of goodwill.

16:23.960 --> 16:25.240
I'll throw it in the canal.

16:28.720 --> 16:30.200
Canals are the idea.

16:30.960 --> 16:31.880
Right, Chang?

16:32.960 --> 16:37.160
♪ I'm the man, I'm the man, I'm the man ♪

16:39.160 --> 16:43.440
♪ I'm the man, the evil man
Yeah, I'm the man ♪

16:45.400 --> 16:49.440
♪ I'm the man, the one you hate
Don't you understand? ♪

16:49.520 --> 16:51.040
♪ The evil man ♪

16:51.600 --> 16:56.880
♪ I'm the man, I'm the man
I'm the man, yeah ♪

16:58.440 --> 17:01.360
I'm sorry for calling the meeting here,
but the location is part of the deal.

17:01.440 --> 17:02.360
[Arthur] What fucking deal?

17:04.800 --> 17:07.240
How does it feel
to be barefoot in the mud again, Pol?

17:07.320 --> 17:09.240
Makes me feel young.

17:09.319 --> 17:10.720
What fucking deal?

17:10.800 --> 17:11.680
[Tommy] Four boats,

17:12.400 --> 17:16.280
four days, up the Grand Union
from Poplar to here.

17:16.359 --> 17:17.960
Half the cargo is coal...

17:18.920 --> 17:20.400
and underneath the coal...

17:21.319 --> 17:22.480
pure opium crystal.

17:23.240 --> 17:24.319
Opium?

17:25.200 --> 17:26.480
I vote against it.

17:27.240 --> 17:28.560
They can't use trucks

17:28.640 --> 17:31.040
because the Chinese drivers
get stopped by the police.

17:31.119 --> 17:32.400
They need to get it out of London

17:32.480 --> 17:35.120
because all the warehouses
are being searched by Customs.

17:35.200 --> 17:38.520
The seven tons is bound for San Francisco,

17:38.600 --> 17:41.760
but the outward ship doesn't sail
for seven days from Liverpool.

17:41.840 --> 17:43.320
They need somewhere safe to store it.

17:43.400 --> 17:47.400
All we have to do is take it up the canal
and keep it here for a week.

17:47.480 --> 17:50.800
We don't fuck with the Chinese
though, Tom. Dad always said it.

17:50.880 --> 17:54.840
Ask yourself, would he turn down £250,000

17:54.920 --> 17:59.240
to drive four boats up the canal
with no prospect of inspection?

18:00.960 --> 18:04.120
My vote's against it, Tom.
Hmm? Mmm-mmm.

18:04.200 --> 18:07.600
Polly... £250,000.

18:07.680 --> 18:10.880
That's half of what
Michael lost in Chicago.

18:11.520 --> 18:14.160
I will ask him
to take charge of this business.

18:14.680 --> 18:17.240
Michael's position
will be reinstated in the company?

18:18.400 --> 18:20.320
His period of quarantine will be over.

18:25.960 --> 18:27.200
Think about it, brother.

18:27.280 --> 18:31.520
Four boats sailing up the cut,
smelling of woodsmoke and bacon.

18:34.000 --> 18:38.320
Which one of Charlie's Gypsy
didicoy friends do you trust, Tom, eh?

18:38.400 --> 18:40.960
With a cargo worth a million pounds?

18:41.040 --> 18:43.360
I've already made provision.
I'm needed at a meeting.

18:43.440 --> 18:44.560
Let's vote.

18:46.360 --> 18:47.520
Those in favour?

18:55.080 --> 18:55.920
[Arthur] Mmm.

18:58.080 --> 18:59.560
[Tommy] Motion carried.

18:59.640 --> 19:05.040
Arthur, tell Charlie we need four boats,
four tons of coal before it gets dark.

19:05.120 --> 19:06.440
They sail south tonight.

19:08.080 --> 19:12.560
And don't forget to go to the Bull Ring
and get them three songbirds, Arthur.

19:12.640 --> 19:13.680
Yes, Tommy.

19:14.880 --> 19:15.880
Fuck!

19:17.720 --> 19:19.640
[inhaling heavily through teeth]

19:31.040 --> 19:32.360
What have you heard, Pol?

19:34.520 --> 19:36.760
The man you cut went to the police.

19:38.880 --> 19:40.120
But we dealt with it.

19:43.400 --> 19:44.680
Was she with him?

19:46.040 --> 19:48.240
If she was,
it would be your fault, Arthur.

19:49.800 --> 19:53.400
But they say his face is so badly cut,
he's hard to look at.

19:53.480 --> 19:54.880
So I would say not.

19:56.360 --> 20:00.560
I would also say
it is time to give up on Linda.

20:00.640 --> 20:01.640
[Arthur inhales deeply]

20:02.920 --> 20:07.680
Find someone else
who might be able to put your fires out.

20:19.800 --> 20:21.320
But I can't, though, Pol.

20:24.200 --> 20:25.400
I fucking can't!

20:29.400 --> 20:30.560
And that's it.

20:32.280 --> 20:33.680
That's it.

20:49.200 --> 20:50.120
Whisky?

20:50.640 --> 20:51.640
Thank you, no.

20:59.400 --> 21:00.240
[Tommy sighs]

21:03.240 --> 21:06.560
For reasons I can't divulge,
I need to keep Jimmy McCavern alive.

21:07.640 --> 21:09.840
But I've already got
a time and a place for the killing.

21:11.000 --> 21:11.960
You see...

21:13.560 --> 21:16.760
a little alleyway by a shipyard canteen.

21:16.840 --> 21:19.600
A girl called Karen who hates him,
who will give him up.

21:20.160 --> 21:24.840
I have the sound of cranes
and winches to cover the gunshot.

21:24.920 --> 21:26.920
I've got a Bentley to get me away.

21:27.000 --> 21:27.880
[Tommy inhales sharply]

21:27.960 --> 21:29.560
The war with the Billy Boys is postponed.

21:29.640 --> 21:32.240
We've made peace.
We're gonna do business together.

21:33.240 --> 21:36.000
When that business is done,
he's all yours.

21:36.640 --> 21:40.000
You can avenge the death of your son
in any way you see fit.

21:40.720 --> 21:42.640
You mean when you say.

21:42.720 --> 21:44.760
When you check
that little stopwatch you've got

21:45.600 --> 21:47.760
that controls the turning of the Earth.

21:48.760 --> 21:49.680
Yeah.

21:51.200 --> 21:52.920
And then you will marry
and you will settle.

21:53.000 --> 21:55.360
Marry? Marry who, Mr Shelby?

21:56.600 --> 21:57.440
[scoffs]

21:58.000 --> 21:59.560
Just let me understand you.

22:00.160 --> 22:02.960
Do you mean
that Polly is part of this deal?

22:04.560 --> 22:05.480
Yeah.

22:06.760 --> 22:07.640
[clears throat]

22:09.560 --> 22:11.480
Well, Holy Lord God.

22:11.960 --> 22:16.360
Tommy Shelby OBE,
does your vanity have no limits?

22:16.440 --> 22:18.920
I believe it's called
the ego these days. [clears throat]

22:19.000 --> 22:19.840
I read books.

22:20.400 --> 22:22.920
You sit in your throne
and you instruct Polly Gray,

22:23.000 --> 22:25.160
who is of far richer blood than you,

22:25.240 --> 22:28.160
as to when she can
and when she can't marry.

22:28.240 --> 22:29.920
Oh, no, she instructs herself.

22:30.840 --> 22:32.680
She has her own strategies.

22:32.760 --> 22:34.360
And we are of the same blood.

22:34.440 --> 22:37.680
She will marry you,
but only if you agree to postpone

22:37.760 --> 22:40.920
any attack on McCavern
until this business is done.

22:41.000 --> 22:44.640
So, she is some young Gypsy bride
that's yours to give away.

22:45.600 --> 22:48.600
Young she is,
when she's barefoot on the cobbles.

22:49.440 --> 22:51.800
What about a dowry, then, Mr Shelby?

22:51.880 --> 22:53.120
If it's gonna be done in the old way,

22:53.200 --> 22:55.960
well, you know,
you throw in a few coloured ponies or...

22:56.040 --> 22:57.800
I'm having an event at me house.

22:58.560 --> 22:59.800
You are invited.

23:00.400 --> 23:01.840
Polly will be there.

23:02.760 --> 23:06.840
There will be candles
and violins and dancing.

23:07.440 --> 23:10.200
Polly wants you
to propose in the proper way,

23:10.280 --> 23:12.640
and then she will give you
her terms of acceptance.

23:12.720 --> 23:15.400
Inviting you for this purpose
was Polly's idea.

23:23.200 --> 23:24.760
-You can't read?
-I don't read.

23:25.760 --> 23:27.480
-It's Swan Lake.
-Ballet?

23:28.120 --> 23:30.200
Yeah. Apparently, it's about love.

23:31.400 --> 23:35.560
Polly says that for now,
love must defeat revenge.

23:55.000 --> 23:56.160
[Tommy reading indistinctly]

23:58.600 --> 24:03.280
"As a result of the greed and the excess
of a small number of bankers,

24:03.360 --> 24:06.360
financiers and other feckless gamblers..."

24:06.440 --> 24:07.600
[crowd] Hear, hear.

24:07.680 --> 24:10.640
"...this comprehensive document,
pleading for government intervention

24:10.720 --> 24:12.440
in all areas of economic life,

24:13.320 --> 24:15.520
represents not just socialism,

24:16.320 --> 24:17.480
but a new breed...

24:18.560 --> 24:20.080
of national socialism."

24:20.160 --> 24:21.520
[crowd murmuring]

24:21.600 --> 24:25.040
"And I believe... I believe
that the leaders of my own party

24:25.600 --> 24:28.040
have been very foolish to reject it."

24:28.120 --> 24:29.280
[indistinct chatter]

24:29.360 --> 24:30.240
[Tommy clears throat]

24:30.360 --> 24:34.320
♪ Albert shows, no reprieve ♪

24:34.400 --> 24:38.400
♪ Albert shows, no reprieve ♪

24:38.480 --> 24:42.360
♪ Albert shows, no reprieve ♪

24:42.920 --> 24:47.920
♪ Albert shows, no reprieve ♪

24:49.160 --> 24:53.760
♪ And for each man and woman hung ♪

24:54.920 --> 24:59.360
♪ The last hangman's morality sung ♪

25:09.160 --> 25:10.000
[grunts]

25:11.880 --> 25:15.400
How on earth did you get a ballet company
to come to your bloody house?

25:16.960 --> 25:18.440
It's an independent dance company

25:19.000 --> 25:21.040
dedicated to bringing ballet
to the people.

25:22.000 --> 25:23.280
We share a philosophy.

25:23.800 --> 25:25.120
I'm a patron.

25:25.200 --> 25:26.040
[Mosley clears throat]

25:26.520 --> 25:30.080
I also gave them a lot of money.
[inhales sharply]

25:30.720 --> 25:31.560
[Mosley] Hmm.

25:33.760 --> 25:37.480
And this date is your wife's birthday.

25:39.320 --> 25:40.320
Yeah.

25:41.120 --> 25:42.280
The party is for her.

25:45.800 --> 25:47.920
And she likes ballet, your wife?

25:49.560 --> 25:50.400
[scoffs]

25:55.120 --> 25:56.200
Why wouldn't she?

25:57.680 --> 26:01.400
It's just... Well, you see,
I did some research into her.

26:03.520 --> 26:05.080
Into her past.

26:05.160 --> 26:08.520
If you want to buy her a gift...
she likes diamonds.

26:13.640 --> 26:16.160
Now that we're going to be
conquering the world together,

26:16.240 --> 26:17.720
we need to have no secrets.

26:18.560 --> 26:21.080
We should know each other's weaknesses.

26:23.320 --> 26:25.920
Your wife has led an interesting life.

26:27.920 --> 26:30.720
It may even be possible
that as a younger man in Birmingham,

26:30.800 --> 26:32.720
I came across her.

26:34.680 --> 26:38.080
My friends and I would sometimes go
to nightclubs in the south of town.

26:39.320 --> 26:43.160
Well, if you recognize her,
maybe you can talk about old times, eh?

26:44.880 --> 26:45.800
Maybe,

26:46.440 --> 26:50.280
if we have met before, your wife and I
could even renew our acquaintance.

26:52.520 --> 26:54.840
I am invited to stay the night, yes?

26:56.680 --> 27:00.320
I, too, have done some research,
Sir Oswald.

27:01.840 --> 27:04.440
Yeah, I researched your wife

27:05.560 --> 27:07.560
and your wife's younger sister,

27:08.320 --> 27:10.840
and your wife's stepmother, Lady Curzon.

27:11.400 --> 27:13.200
All of whom you are fucking.

27:14.240 --> 27:16.560
If such things were to take place
on a narrow boat,

27:16.640 --> 27:18.360
the church would get involved.

27:20.160 --> 27:21.200
[softly] But...

27:22.040 --> 27:24.160
it's not happening on a narrow boat.

27:25.760 --> 27:26.800
[Tommy] No.

27:27.360 --> 27:31.040
It's taking place in your apartment,
in your country house,

27:31.120 --> 27:35.480
sometimes even in your office here
in the House of Commons.

27:35.560 --> 27:36.400
[clicks tongue]

27:37.560 --> 27:39.240
So, no secrets. And yes.

27:40.080 --> 27:42.680
Yes, you are invited to stay the night

27:43.520 --> 27:45.880
with whichever member of your family
finds favour.

27:47.200 --> 27:49.000
Now, if you don't mind,
I was about to leave.

27:49.080 --> 27:50.520
I need to lock up me office.

28:01.800 --> 28:03.480
Actually, I will come alone.

28:05.120 --> 28:07.840
In society, you are judged
by your hospitality.

28:07.920 --> 28:09.960
I will expect adventure.

28:20.640 --> 28:22.880
[whispering] Such rogues
we are, aren't we?

28:24.680 --> 28:26.680
Sing like songbirds in the House.

28:27.560 --> 28:28.640
And then afterwards,

28:28.720 --> 28:32.120
relieve ourselves in the bodies
of whomever we choose.

28:35.240 --> 28:38.680
Two men for whom forbidding is forbidden.

28:40.120 --> 28:41.560
Should be quite a party.

28:51.000 --> 28:51.840
[door closes]

28:59.920 --> 29:00.960
[sighs]

29:23.440 --> 29:26.440
[Grace] You have to listen
to the voices that you hear.

29:27.360 --> 29:29.200
Do what they tell you to do.

29:31.520 --> 29:34.600
You don't even have to rub the lamp
any more to summon the genie.

29:36.920 --> 29:38.920
It wasn't the blue stone, Tommy.

29:40.400 --> 29:41.600
It was you.

29:43.800 --> 29:45.000
It was you.

30:08.240 --> 30:09.080
[sighs]

30:59.800 --> 31:00.760
Who is it?

31:01.720 --> 31:03.680
It's Tommy's car outside. It's him.

31:04.200 --> 31:05.160
I'll get it.

31:12.840 --> 31:13.760
What's happened?

31:14.320 --> 31:15.920
Nothing's happened. I'm all right.

31:16.000 --> 31:17.680
-[clears throat]
-Come in.

31:20.760 --> 31:22.080
Do you want a drink?

31:22.160 --> 31:24.080
-No.
-No?

31:24.160 --> 31:27.320
No. I have some information
for the intelligence officer.

31:28.200 --> 31:29.960
Our conversations with Mosley.

31:30.680 --> 31:33.520
He's planning to put forward
proposals on building works.

31:34.240 --> 31:35.600
He, um... [clears throat]

31:36.560 --> 31:39.240
He wants the communists
to consider his new party as fraternal,

31:39.320 --> 31:43.160
which means his activities are now a part
of your official remit. Yeah?

31:43.240 --> 31:46.120
[chuckles] Mr Shelby, it's 2:00 a.m.
You can make your report any time.

31:46.200 --> 31:48.520
-Why don't you stay tonight?
-No.

31:52.600 --> 31:54.480
I'll leave you two to...

31:54.560 --> 31:55.640
Yes.

31:55.720 --> 31:56.560
Good night.

31:56.640 --> 31:57.480
[clears throat]

32:07.920 --> 32:08.800
[breathing heavily]

32:10.800 --> 32:14.000
Uh, I stood on a bridge tonight, Ada.

32:14.880 --> 32:16.280
And I looked down...

32:18.000 --> 32:19.520
and Grace was there.

32:21.160 --> 32:22.440
But she was still alive.

32:22.520 --> 32:23.840
Tom, have you still
been taking laudanum?

32:23.920 --> 32:26.600
And the fucking name of the barge
was the January.

32:28.840 --> 32:30.160
Our dad's boat.

32:30.240 --> 32:32.640
The boat I was born on.
We've never gotten off it.

32:33.360 --> 32:35.720
We've never gotten off it
and we never fucking will.

32:38.760 --> 32:41.160
Dr Brooke said that you never arrived

32:41.240 --> 32:42.920
-for your appointment, Tom.
-No.

32:44.000 --> 32:46.280
There is nothing in his books
of any use to a man like me.

32:46.800 --> 32:51.560
They talk about guilt. Eh?
Guilt. What fucking guilt?

32:51.640 --> 32:54.360
-The black barge.
-No. No, that's not it.

32:54.440 --> 32:55.280
That's not it.

32:55.360 --> 32:58.160
He had it right.
Mosley had it right. He said,

32:58.240 --> 33:01.760
"Forbidding is forbidden to us."
We can do anything.

33:01.840 --> 33:03.360
Nothing can stop us.

33:04.240 --> 33:07.120
But there is a part of me
that is unfamiliar to myself...

33:09.240 --> 33:10.840
and I keep finding meself there.

33:12.840 --> 33:15.000
And only the January can get me away.

33:18.360 --> 33:20.760
At least try the doctors again, Tom.

33:25.080 --> 33:28.880
Well, then at least throw away your opium.
It's that that causes the visions.

33:28.960 --> 33:30.840
Just throw it away.

33:30.920 --> 33:32.280
While it's there, it's a temptation.

33:32.360 --> 33:33.520
-[Tommy sighs]
-Hmm?

33:34.000 --> 33:35.520
How much have you got left?

33:36.520 --> 33:37.720
Seven tons.

33:38.760 --> 33:40.560
-Seven tons?
-Yep.

33:46.560 --> 33:48.120
I'd hate for it to run out, Ada.

33:49.760 --> 33:50.600
[scoffs]

33:54.200 --> 33:55.080
[sighs]

34:00.240 --> 34:01.480
Hey, do me a favour.

34:04.400 --> 34:05.880
When that kid of yours arrives...

34:07.760 --> 34:08.880
keep it away from me.

34:24.760 --> 34:26.080
A fucking ballet?

34:27.360 --> 34:28.880
He wants to impress somebody.

34:29.560 --> 34:30.880
[Michael] And I'm invited?

34:31.480 --> 34:32.400
You and Gina.

34:34.280 --> 34:35.239
Why?

34:37.040 --> 34:40.719
Because he wants to give you the chance
to come back properly.

34:43.280 --> 34:44.120
[sniffles]

34:52.239 --> 34:54.000
-Coal haulage?
-Yeah.

34:54.639 --> 34:58.639
Tommy wants you to reopen those books
and become managing director.

34:59.719 --> 35:03.560
So I've come back from Detroit
to become a coal man.

35:04.840 --> 35:07.760
The first delivery is bound
for San Francisco.

35:09.000 --> 35:10.120
But if it works,

35:10.960 --> 35:13.760
Tommy thinks he can find
distribution for it here.

35:16.120 --> 35:17.320
And this, um...

35:17.960 --> 35:18.960
this coal.

35:20.120 --> 35:21.840
-Is it snow white?
-No.

35:23.200 --> 35:24.480
Golden brown.

35:27.280 --> 35:28.480
Fuck.

35:31.520 --> 35:33.240
This is your opportunity, Michael.

35:34.680 --> 35:36.120
There is more money in this

35:36.680 --> 35:40.800
than there is in all the other parts
of our business put together.

35:54.560 --> 35:56.840
Tommy knows what opium does to people.

35:56.920 --> 35:58.880
Tommy knows what whiskey does to people.

35:59.720 --> 36:01.560
He got an OBE for selling it.

36:05.240 --> 36:06.640
I'll speak to Gina.

36:08.240 --> 36:09.600
[scoffs] You'll what?

36:10.560 --> 36:12.120
I'll consult my wife.

36:14.000 --> 36:17.960
Your father ran this business for a bit.
1901.

36:18.640 --> 36:21.520
And he shipped coal, real coal. Just coal.

36:22.280 --> 36:28.160
And his fingernails and his eyelids
and his ears were black with it.

36:28.720 --> 36:30.800
And the merchants
would offer them one price

36:31.360 --> 36:34.280
and then only pay half,
because they could.

36:35.160 --> 36:37.280
And that was wrong, Michael.

37:01.240 --> 37:02.840
Run your hands through it,

37:04.480 --> 37:06.160
get it under your skin,

37:07.400 --> 37:11.080
and then see if Gina
will let you lay a finger on her.

37:19.000 --> 37:23.120
I think golden brown is more to her taste.

37:25.280 --> 37:28.600
Especially when you tell her
how much money you're going to earn.

37:36.080 --> 37:36.920
[door opens]

37:40.120 --> 37:40.960
[door closes]

37:50.080 --> 37:52.720
Now we're in business together,
I should ask,

37:52.800 --> 37:56.000
which foot do you
kick the ball with, Mr Shelby?

37:56.080 --> 37:57.320
[Tommy] I have no religion.

37:58.840 --> 38:00.040
Some nights I wish I had.

38:01.160 --> 38:02.240
He's kin?

38:03.360 --> 38:04.280
Yep.

38:05.760 --> 38:07.200
And the simple fellow?

38:08.400 --> 38:10.920
He's a lot less simple
than you might at first think.

38:12.760 --> 38:14.080
Do you trust them?

38:20.200 --> 38:22.040
Right. So I take a boatload.

38:23.120 --> 38:24.360
[Tommy clears throat] Well...

38:24.440 --> 38:27.960
Ten sacks to start with,
so you can test the market.

38:28.480 --> 38:29.920
Then we'll deal in boatloads.

38:30.600 --> 38:32.360
Cash payment on loading.

38:33.160 --> 38:34.520
Ten thousand pound.

38:35.760 --> 38:37.720
Well, for that amount,
it will have to be a cheque.

38:38.280 --> 38:39.400
Don't take cheques.

38:43.200 --> 38:44.400
It'll be a cheque.

38:48.360 --> 38:50.080
I will take a cheque if it's guaranteed

38:50.160 --> 38:52.600
by our mutual friend
in London, Mr Mosley.

39:02.720 --> 39:03.680
[claps hands]

39:03.760 --> 39:04.640
[laughs]

39:05.960 --> 39:08.000
Well, who'd ever have thought
I'd be doing business

39:08.080 --> 39:11.480
with fucking Gypsy Catholic scum?

39:13.440 --> 39:15.520
Yeah, who'd have thought, eh, Charlie?

39:16.920 --> 39:18.280
[Charlie] Who would have thought it?

39:18.960 --> 39:20.200
Ah, but you're okay.

39:20.840 --> 39:23.800
[Tommy] Yeah, I'm only okay
until I'm not okay.

39:25.320 --> 39:26.720
And then I'm really not.

39:28.920 --> 39:31.160
Delivery in seven days.

39:33.520 --> 39:34.800
Cheque guaranteed.

39:34.880 --> 39:38.200
Won't your Chinese friends
expect the seven tons that leaves London

39:38.280 --> 39:40.560
to still be seven tons
when it reaches Liverpool?

39:41.160 --> 39:42.920
You leave that to me, Mr McCavern.

39:43.560 --> 39:46.880
Oh, you mean you're bold enough
to skim the Chinese? [chuckles]

39:49.720 --> 39:52.320
You have some kind of death wish,
Mr Shelby?

40:06.200 --> 40:07.640
[orchestra tuning]

40:11.080 --> 40:13.760
An evening with a tribe of Gypsies.

40:15.080 --> 40:15.920
[sighs]

40:16.840 --> 40:19.520
When you've unpacked,
there should be a girl laid on for you.

40:20.840 --> 40:22.400
Mr Shelby is a socialist

40:22.480 --> 40:25.040
and believes in
equality of service for all classes.

40:35.920 --> 40:39.840
According to the invitation...
there will be an interval at 9:00.

40:39.920 --> 40:41.840
Say that you're feeling tired
and we'll leave.

40:43.360 --> 40:46.840
Well... if you see a duke,
introduce me.

40:47.600 --> 40:49.280
[Michael] My God, at last.

40:49.880 --> 40:51.640
-Something that you like about England.
-[scoffs]

40:54.560 --> 40:55.600
Gina,

40:56.280 --> 40:57.520
I've been made an offer...

41:00.160 --> 41:01.600
to come back into the company.

41:02.440 --> 41:03.680
Michael,

41:03.760 --> 41:06.680
we agreed the baby will be born
in New York. Remember?

41:06.760 --> 41:08.120
The job is haulage.

41:09.120 --> 41:10.760
Supply. Transport.

41:12.960 --> 41:14.080
Opium.

41:18.240 --> 41:20.520
-Tommy has made contact--
-Tommy.

41:22.040 --> 41:23.280
Tommy has made contact

41:23.360 --> 41:26.520
with Chinese suppliers
who have plantations in the Afghan hills.

41:27.880 --> 41:28.880
Pure grade.

41:30.800 --> 41:34.240
We'll take delivery
and ship it all over Europe.

41:35.840 --> 41:37.200
You mean heroin?

41:38.720 --> 41:39.680
Yes.

41:42.680 --> 41:44.200
And how much would you make?

41:45.920 --> 41:47.440
Conservative estimate,

41:47.520 --> 41:50.760
three shipments a year
from Shanghai, seven tons each.

41:51.440 --> 41:54.920
Stand to make approximately
a million pounds. Per annum.

41:57.120 --> 41:58.360
The company will make three.

42:01.680 --> 42:02.520
[Gina sighs]

42:02.600 --> 42:04.720
We could go to New York
whenever we wanted.

42:06.040 --> 42:07.680
On our own fucking plane.

42:11.280 --> 42:12.960
-But we always have to come back, right?
-Yes.

42:14.400 --> 42:16.480
For a million pounds a year, we do.

42:19.240 --> 42:21.080
What happens if you get caught?

42:22.040 --> 42:23.360
Tommy has friends.

42:25.000 --> 42:27.920
If a ship gets stopped,
it'll be the Chinese who hang.

42:31.040 --> 42:32.160
Think about it, Gina.

42:34.240 --> 42:36.120
When we move into our house,

42:37.240 --> 42:41.160
our room for entertaining
will be twice this size.

42:45.080 --> 42:46.320
Will it, now?

42:49.400 --> 42:51.000
[Michael] Magazines say that

42:51.600 --> 42:54.880
it's all straight lines and simplicity
in the 1930s.

42:56.520 --> 42:57.800
Deco is dead.

43:00.960 --> 43:04.120
We'll be able
to afford dukes and duchesses.

43:05.760 --> 43:09.120
And maybe...
maybe a princess or two.

43:11.280 --> 43:13.520
And the painting on the wall
will be of you.

43:15.320 --> 43:17.360
If Tommy Shelby will be gone,

43:18.360 --> 43:20.960
then it will be Michael Gray
arranging the ballet.

43:23.360 --> 43:24.680
Where will Tommy be?

43:26.720 --> 43:28.200
Where he wants to go to most.

43:31.480 --> 43:32.560
Ah.

43:34.240 --> 43:35.320
There.

43:36.960 --> 43:38.040
A lord.

43:38.840 --> 43:41.800
Actually, I think Mr Mosley's a baronet.

43:48.120 --> 43:49.920
Where the fuck is Tommy, anyway?

43:51.280 --> 43:52.640
[panting]

43:59.560 --> 44:00.400
[both moaning]

44:05.720 --> 44:06.800
Tommy.

44:07.760 --> 44:10.560
My house. My wife.

44:12.080 --> 44:13.240
Let them wait.

44:17.680 --> 44:18.880
Sir Oswald.

44:21.320 --> 44:23.240
Do I not get announced?

44:24.160 --> 44:28.720
Mr Shelby asked me to tell you that
he's busy with the catering preparations

44:28.800 --> 44:30.720
and will be joining you shortly.

44:32.280 --> 44:35.160
In the meantime,
and while you are waiting,

44:35.240 --> 44:38.160
we have opium, cocaine and brandy.

44:39.920 --> 44:42.880
I don't use opium. Or cocaine.

44:43.440 --> 44:45.920
And brandy is for after dinner,
not before.

44:47.720 --> 44:50.640
I also have a list of options
for the end of the evening.

44:51.560 --> 44:55.280
You will notice
that the maids wear name tags.

44:56.080 --> 44:57.760
We hired them specially.

44:58.960 --> 45:00.800
For those guests staying the night,

45:01.920 --> 45:06.080
all things are available...
except the ballerinas.

45:09.000 --> 45:11.120
And who, might I ask, are you?

45:12.680 --> 45:15.760
I am a queen amongst the Romanies.

45:16.760 --> 45:19.480
And I, too, am unavailable.

45:28.760 --> 45:32.440
Lizzie... there's something
I didn't tell you about this evening.

45:33.760 --> 45:35.120
Something about our guest.

45:36.080 --> 45:37.200
Mosley.

45:39.480 --> 45:42.560
It's possible that you've met him before.

45:43.680 --> 45:44.600
Before when?

45:45.720 --> 45:48.400
[smacks lips]
Before you became who you are.

45:51.600 --> 45:53.040
Would you even remember him?

45:54.640 --> 45:56.040
Will he remember you?

45:58.360 --> 46:01.040
All I remember is
I drank too much champagne.

46:01.640 --> 46:03.120
And I wasn't taking cash.

46:06.280 --> 46:07.560
Lizzie.

46:10.720 --> 46:11.920
It's a pile of bodies...

46:13.040 --> 46:14.080
floating by.

46:15.360 --> 46:16.520
Let 'em go, Lizzie.

46:18.680 --> 46:19.680
Let 'em go.

46:23.520 --> 46:25.400
So, that's why you brought me in here.

46:25.960 --> 46:27.360
To lay your claim.

46:29.240 --> 46:30.080
Yeah.

46:34.120 --> 46:36.240
Well, it's a start, I suppose.

46:38.280 --> 46:40.400
He lays a fucking hand on you,

46:41.280 --> 46:43.760
he will be meat for Johnny Dogs.

46:43.840 --> 46:44.800
[door opens]

46:48.720 --> 46:50.560
[Mosley] You were indisposed
when I arrived.

46:58.560 --> 47:02.560
In society, you greet a guest.
You don't leave them hanging...

47:03.520 --> 47:05.520
looking around like a fucking dog.

47:06.280 --> 47:09.200
[clears throat] Before we join the others,
I have some business.

47:09.960 --> 47:10.960
I need a signature.

47:11.840 --> 47:14.720
By the way, your brandy
before dinner thing amuses me,

47:14.800 --> 47:16.760
but none of the maids are of interest.

47:17.520 --> 47:19.640
And I despise the use of drugs.

47:21.520 --> 47:23.720
Your strategies are very transparent.

47:25.080 --> 47:28.200
I'm involved in a transaction
with Jimmy McCavern,

47:28.280 --> 47:30.120
your acquaintance from the north.

47:30.760 --> 47:32.640
I have no idea who you mean.

47:32.720 --> 47:35.120
I don't trust him.
He wants to pay by cheque.

47:35.680 --> 47:38.560
I need your signature
as a guarantor on the transaction,

47:38.640 --> 47:40.800
should his cheque fail to be honoured.

47:40.880 --> 47:42.560
The sum is £10,000.

47:42.640 --> 47:45.000
And what is it he is buying from you?

47:45.080 --> 47:48.120
Gin distillery. He's buying me old one.
I'm buying a new one.

47:49.640 --> 47:50.480
Hmm.

47:53.880 --> 47:58.000
So, not only is the truce holding,
but you two are actually doing business.

47:58.640 --> 48:00.960
Yeah. But I still don't trust his cheques.

48:03.720 --> 48:05.880
If I sign a cheque guarantee for this man,

48:05.960 --> 48:08.520
it is proof of a connection
between me and him.

48:08.600 --> 48:11.200
Something you could later use against me.

48:12.880 --> 48:14.760
[grunts] Why would I
want to move against you?

48:32.040 --> 48:34.080
You're curious about my weaknesses.

48:36.240 --> 48:41.120
And you have learned it's not cocaine...
not maids.

48:50.680 --> 48:53.160
But now you will learn my weakness...

48:53.920 --> 48:56.240
is a tendency to trust people.
Do you have a pen?

49:10.480 --> 49:11.320
[clears throat]

49:12.800 --> 49:13.960
Mr Shelby.

49:16.320 --> 49:19.280
I know you had no classical education,
but I've just realised

49:19.360 --> 49:22.640
you are the perfect balance
between the gods Dionysus and Apollo.

49:23.240 --> 49:27.600
Irrational frenzy
controlled by reason and self-reflection.

49:30.360 --> 49:32.560
Do you know
the work of Friedrich Nietzsche?

49:33.520 --> 49:35.000
-No.
-Freud?

49:35.760 --> 49:36.800
Yes.

49:37.480 --> 49:38.320
Ah.

49:43.440 --> 49:44.560
There.

49:45.480 --> 49:47.040
Your guarantee of trust.

49:49.040 --> 49:52.080
Now, perhaps you could introduce me
to your wonderful wife.

49:56.960 --> 49:58.480
So, did you know?

49:58.960 --> 49:59.800
What?

50:00.920 --> 50:02.200
Oh, that tonight's special guest

50:02.280 --> 50:04.520
might have fucked you
when you were a nightclub hostess?

50:05.600 --> 50:06.600
Yeah.

50:08.200 --> 50:11.040
Lizzie, if we were to
strike from our guest list

50:11.120 --> 50:13.240
-every man in Birmingham who you--
-Fuck.

50:15.920 --> 50:18.680
-Yes or no?
-Fucking yes. Shit.

50:23.120 --> 50:26.360
Sir Oswald, this is my wife, Elizabeth.

50:26.440 --> 50:28.600
Lizzie, Sir Oswald Mosley.

50:30.880 --> 50:34.800
Since we all appear to know,
and since knowledge is permission,

50:35.520 --> 50:39.240
I'm sure, Mr Shelby,
in the spirit of our honest relationship,

50:39.320 --> 50:40.400
you won't mind me saying,

50:40.960 --> 50:43.480
it was a bottle of champagne
and an evening well spent.

50:45.760 --> 50:48.680
Actually, it was an evening wasted.

50:50.520 --> 50:52.680
For the champagne and brandy
you bought me.

50:52.760 --> 50:56.360
As I recall, it was the booze that
put you to sleep a little prematurely.

50:57.200 --> 51:02.280
Ladies and gentlemen...
the dance is about to begin.

51:06.520 --> 51:07.800
Mr Mosley,

51:08.560 --> 51:10.320
a toast, if I may.

51:11.640 --> 51:13.040
To the end of our deal.

51:13.600 --> 51:15.360
And the beginning of something more.

51:16.760 --> 51:18.080
Happy birthday, Lizzie.

51:22.320 --> 51:23.320
This way.

51:26.160 --> 51:28.160
[orchestral music playing]

51:57.080 --> 51:58.040
[snoring]

52:51.680 --> 52:54.200
Polly Gray, Gypsy queen...

52:54.880 --> 52:59.240
will you marry me,
a poor commoner who loves you?

53:18.080 --> 53:18.920
[sighs]

53:31.320 --> 53:32.160
[grunts]

53:56.160 --> 53:57.280
Let's fuck

53:58.560 --> 54:00.000
before the swan dies.

54:03.200 --> 54:04.280
[engine revving]

54:28.160 --> 54:29.000
[exhales sharply]

54:30.920 --> 54:32.840
I heard there was a family occasion.

54:38.000 --> 54:39.560
[Arthur] Look, I'm sorry, Linda.

54:40.600 --> 54:42.360
That animal inside me,

54:43.160 --> 54:45.240
it comes out and I can't stop it.

54:47.680 --> 54:49.000
Fuck, Linda.

54:49.840 --> 54:50.840
Without you, I...

54:51.680 --> 54:52.880
Come inside, please.

54:54.880 --> 54:56.680
His name was Frederick.

54:57.240 --> 54:59.120
All we ever did was talk, Arthur.

54:59.200 --> 55:00.480
He just listened.

55:02.200 --> 55:04.200
And now he has no face.

55:12.760 --> 55:15.720
He's as ugly on the outside
as you are on the inside.

55:24.600 --> 55:26.560
May you Peaky Blinders all rot...

55:27.760 --> 55:29.200
in fucking hell.

55:32.080 --> 55:33.040
[gun fires]

55:33.120 --> 55:33.960
[panting]

55:40.800 --> 55:41.880
[Tommy] Arthur.

55:41.960 --> 55:43.480
[audience applauding inside]

56:14.920 --> 56:16.920
[theme song playing]

56:31.040 --> 56:35.240
♪ On a gathering storm
Comes a tall handsome man ♪

56:35.320 --> 56:39.760
♪ In a dusty black coat
With a red right hand ♪

56:47.440 --> 56:52.040
♪ A shadow is cast wherever he stands ♪
